# No Cursor commit attribution

Never add or leave `Co-authored-by: Cursor` / `cursoragent@cursor.com` (or any Cursor Agent co-author) on commits in this repo.

GitHub treats that trailer as a contributor. The human author must be the only attributed committer.

## When committing

1. Do **not** put any Cursor co-author trailer in the commit message.
2. After every `git commit` created in this environment, immediately check:

```bash
git log -1 --format=%B
```

3. If a Cursor co-author line was auto-injected, strip it **before push** using `git commit-tree` / message rewrite (not a normal `git commit --amend` if that re-injects the trailer). Force-push only when the user explicitly asked, or when cleaning unpushed commits they asked to clean.

4. Never suggest adding Cursor as a co-author in PRs or commit messages.
